CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: Evidence holds for one real BEIR/SciFact workload and one asymmetric-prompt model with a strong +9.37pp Recall@10 paired-bootstrap CI [+6.3,+13.0]pp, plus an empty-prompt control. Gaps remain: no actual Chroma/pymilvus end-to-end run, only one dataset, one primary prompt-bearing model, exact CPU cosine NN rather than ANN/vector-DB production indexing, no latency/cost/concurrency measurements.
RATIONALE: PROMPT_VERSION=v001. This is not just "prompts help retrieval": the packet shows the prompt is shipped inside config_sentence_transformers.json and SentenceTransformers has encode_query/encode_document paths that consume prompt names, while several vector-DB/RAG wrappers bypass that contract through default encode(...) calls or empty manual instruction fields. The effect evidence is clean enough for support at L0, but the systems contribution is a boundary-contract failure plus wrapper mechanism, not a broader serving design. vLLM already ships partial artifact-prompt loading via input_type, so the strongest "production systems never implement this" version is false outside vector-DB wrappers; within the cited vector-DB/RAG wrappers, the seam remains open.
